1
00:00:03,177 --> 00:00:06,337
Open Interaction Center, My voicemail greeting.

2
00:00:06,337 --> 00:00:10,689
Your greeting is what callers hear before they leave you a message.

3
00:00:10,689 --> 00:00:14,147
If you do not set one, the default greeting is used.

4
00:00:14,675 --> 00:00:17,539
Record with microphone is the default.

5
00:00:17,539 --> 00:00:22,031
Click Record, speak, then click Stop, which is the same button.

6
00:00:22,031 --> 00:00:27,825
If your browser cannot record, the page says so, and you can upload a file instead.

7
00:00:28,290 --> 00:00:32,505
Choose Upload a file to pick an audio file:

8
00:00:32,505 --> 00:00:34,655
M.P.3, wave, O.G.G.

9
00:00:34,655 --> 00:00:38,010
or web M, up to twenty megabytes.

10
00:00:38,473 --> 00:00:41,518
Listen to the Preview, and click Save greeting.

11
00:00:41,518 --> 00:00:46,230
The platform keeps the master copy, and sends it to whichever phone provider

12
00:00:46,230 --> 00:00:47,953
a caller reaches you on.

13
00:00:48,404 --> 00:00:50,888
Remove greeting goes back to the default.

14
00:00:50,888 --> 00:00:54,851
When you have no greeting of your own, callers hear the entry point's

15
00:00:54,851 --> 00:00:59,184
Default voicemail greeting, and when that is empty too, a built-in greeting.

